@startuml
title D-03 Site Group / Site / VendorSystem / Connector Instance / POS Server Topology
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220

actor "Customer / Channel" as Customer

rectangle "Customer Lookup / Payment Scope" {
  component "Site Group\nlookup + payment scope" as SG
}

rectangle "Resolved Operational Boundaries" {
  component "Site A\nreporting, contract,\nVendor PMS mapping,\nPOS routing, operations" as SiteA
  component "Site B\nspecial multi-Site case" as SiteB
}

rectangle "Vendor Integration Configuration" {
  component "VendorSystem\nconfigured Vendor PMS / HCP instance" as VS
  component "AdapterMapping\nSite to vendor object mapping" as Mapping
  component "Adapter codebase\nreusable connector implementation" as Adapter
  component "Connector instance\ndeployed runtime connector" as Connector
}

cloud "Vendor PMS / HCP\nvendor-side objects and sessions" as Vendor
component "Resolved Site POS Server\nfiscal routing target" as POS
component "Management Dashboard\nSite Group + Site views" as Dash

Customer --> SG : chooses / enters payment scope
SG --> SiteA : default one Site Group to one Site
SG --> SiteB : optional multi-Site case

SiteA --> Mapping : configured mapping
SiteB --> Mapping : configured mapping
Mapping --> VS : vendor object belongs to VendorSystem
Connector --> VS : runtime connector for instance
Connector --> Adapter : uses reusable implementation
Connector --> Vendor : live session / tariff / projection

SiteA --> POS : fiscal attribution + routing
SiteB --> POS : fiscal attribution + routing
SiteA --> Dash : operational + financial scope
SiteB --> Dash : operational + financial scope

note bottom of SG
Site Group is customer lookup/payment scope.
User-facing terminology remains open.
end note

note bottom of SiteA
Physical parking lot is not automatically
an ExitPass Site.
end note

note right of Mapping
HCP ParkingLotIndexCode is vendor-side only.
It must not be treated as ExitPass site_id.
end note
@enduml
